timeline
    title local-llm: Past Milestones and Planned Direction
    section Cloud Prototype (Jul 2026)
      2026-07-18 : Project scaffolded against OpenRouter : custom Python CLI, per-session memory, and JSONL usage logging : Qwen2.5-Coder-32B (coding) and DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-32B (reasoning)
      2026-07-20 : Custom React and FastAPI chat frontend added
      2026-07-21 : Custom frontend and backend retired in favor of Open WebUI, run via Docker
    section Local Inference Begins (Aug 2026)
      2026-08-17 : llama.cpp stood up on the laptop's RTX 3060 (6 GB) : Qwen3.6-35B-A3B MoE served via --n-cpu-moe as a parallel evaluation track
      2026-08-23 : Automated GPU telemetry : -ot tensor pinning for Qwen3.8-27B : MTP speculative decoding enabled : llama-test harness added : critical --parallel slot-count bug found and fixed
      2026-08-24 : First multi-prompt MTP speculative decoding measurement, 91.9% acceptance
      2026-08-30 : Correctness benchmarking added against HumanEval, MBPP, and DS-1000 : SQLite-backed results store (llama.db) : Textual terminal dashboard (llama-ui)
    section Hardening and Tooling (Sep 2026)
      2026-09-04 : qwen25c VRAM-resident profile added : system-prompt A/B testing capability added : five defects from a pre-merge code review fixed
      2026-09-05 : Statistical reporting command (llama-report) added with paired significance testing : server build specification finalized ($1,316.10 of a $2,000 ceiling)
      2026-09-06 : Textual dashboard replaced by a browser dashboard (llama-web) reachable behind a Caddy reverse proxy at the same port as Open WebUI
      2026-09-07 : qwen3c serving profile completed and documented
      2026-09-07 : Open WebUI forked and pinned (v0.11.3, git submodule, never merged) : Postgres+pgvector replaces SQLite/Chroma : lllm-frontend/lllm-backend run as host processes, Caddy retired : shell tooling reorganized under scripts/shell/, re-prefixed lllm-
      2026-09-08 : lllm-test/lllm-compare/lllm-report/lllm-tune/lllm-web suite migrated into the Open WebUI fork as its own Benchmarks section : logs/llama.db backfilled into Postgres and retired : CLI fully retired
      2026-09-14 : Open WebUI fork vendored into this repo as a monorepo, submodule retired : permanent hard fork, no upstream sync : tree moved to apps/openwebui and infra/ : serving-layer baseline captured ahead of the shell-to-Python port
      2026-09-14 to 2026-09-17 : Serving layer ported from shell to Python (Phases 2a-2b) : profiles, fingerprint, and launcher moved into the backend and Postgres : env_profile/proc/tune_schedule/tune_probe/serve router rewired to call it in-process instead of shelling out
      2026-09-18 : Shell layer deleted entirely (Phase 2c) : scripts/ removed along with root requirements.txt/.venv : root Makefile (make backend, make frontend) added as the process-lifecycle replacement : ~/.bashrc's shell-sourcing line removed : Serve and Tune verified against real hardware, closing Phase 2
      2026-09-18 (later) : Astro + React + shadcn/ui scaffold added (Phase 3) : apps/web/, Tailwind v4, dark mode, dev-server proxy, make astro : /next preview mount in main.py alongside the SvelteKit app : Vitest and Playwright wired with one smoke test each
      2026-09-18 (later still) : Shared frontend foundation completed (Phase 4) : API layer, auth + route gate, Zustand/TanStack Query, react-i18next, Socket.IO provider, an AppShell/Sidebar on shadcn, and a react-router shell with a Svelte fallback for everything not yet ported
      2026-09-18 (later still, cont.) : Benchmarks surface completed (Phase 5) : Serve, Live, Tests, Compare, Answers, Report, and Tune ported to React, plus a new Profiles CRUD panel the Svelte app never had : DOMPurify added as defense in depth for the two markdown-rendering pages
      2026-09-19 : Public pages completed (Phase 6) : /auth (sign-in, sign-up, LDAP, OAuth, onboarding), /error, /watch, and read-only shared chats at /s/:id : the auth gate now navigates in-app to the new /auth : a Phase 4 bug fixed where backend config was only fetched after a session existed
      2026-09-19 (later) : Workspace surface completed (Phase 7) : Models, Knowledge, Prompts, Skills, and Tools ported to React (with the Functions create link) on a shared kit of toasts, list chrome, and an access-control family : CodeMirror added for the tool editor : a Create-button bug and a dev-server crash under Bun found by testing : untrusted community/import input hardened across the section
      2026-09-27 : Admin surface completed (Phase 8) : Users and Groups, Evaluations, Functions, and all sixteen admin Settings tabs ported to React : Settings rebuilt as a modal host that Phase 10's personal tabs will share : repeated Svelte markup made table-driven (permissions, interface preferences) : CSV-injection, masked-credential and import hardening over the original
      2026-09-27 (later) : Secondary surfaces completed (Phase 9) : Notes (TipTap), Calendar, Automations, Playground, and Channels ported to React : Channels is the first live Socket.IO surface (messages, threads, reactions, typing, unread badges) : the not-yet-ported fallback no longer loops on the dev server
      2026-09-27 (latest) : Chat surface completed (Phase 10) : chat, streaming over Socket.IO, message actions, attachments and / # @ commands, the sidebar chat list, and all twelve personal Settings tabs ported to React : per-chat controls, a sandboxed HTML artifact preview, and the chat header menu : no path is Svelte-only any more, leaving only the Phase 11 cutover
      2026-09-27 (final) : Cutover complete (Phase 11) : first run against a real backend, eight bugs fixed : the backend serves the React app at its root : SvelteKit frontend, upstream Docker and CI deleted : fork renamed to apps/server
      2026-09-28 : Code review of the React frontend (docs/history/code-review.md) : one high and seven medium findings fixed, among them live HTML from other users in channels and shared chats, and 44 settings that were saved but never used : the dev backend now binds loopback by default
    section Native Linux (Oct 2026)
      2026-10-09 : Moved from WSL2 to native Fedora 44 on the same laptop : Docker Engine replaces Docker Desktop : Python 3.12 via uv, backend venv and frontend rebuilt : llama.cpp CUDA build and the old Postgres data still to restore : WSL2-era benchmark numbers marked historical
      2026-10-10 : Repository restructured into one project, Local LLM : docs and agent guide consolidated at the root : backend flattened, package renamed local_llm, WEBUI_* env vars renamed LLLM_* : upstream hub, update check and license server removed : make check mirrors CI : the old Postgres data confirmed lost (no dump existed)
      2026-10-11 : Old plugin source aliased to local_llm at import time instead of rewritten, so every import form and the renamed WEBUI_* names still load
      2026-10-17 : ruff-check gates the whole backend, not just benchmarks/ and tests/ : 166 import blocks sorted and 323 other findings fixed rule by rule, with SQL and string values verified unchanged : max-complexity 25, the 35 inherited functions above it to be refactored rather than exempted : applied migrations excluded
      2026-10-17 (later) : Generated code excluded from linting and formatting : Alembic revisions (ruff), shadcn/ui components (Biome), uv.lock (check-toml) : security scans still cover everything
      2026-10-17 (later still) : The twelve unused vector stores removed, pgvector the only one : their settings and dependencies (opensearch-py, mariadb, elasticsearch, weaviate, pinecone, oracledb) gone : external knowledge connections to Qdrant and Milvus kept
      2026-10-17 (latest) : LDAP sign-in removed : the /ldap route, admin LDAP settings, the sign-in form's LDAP mode and ldap3 gone : unused, and local accounts cover a household install
      2026-10-17 (final) : All 35 functions above the complexity limit dealt with : 33 refactored behind characterization tests (#86 to #124), two deleted with their features : the bugs the tests exposed fixed in separate PRs : the temporary C901 list removed, so max-complexity 25 applies everywhere
      2026-10-19 : Error bars in Compare and Report (Miller, arXiv:2411.00640) : per-problem averaging, Wilson intervals, cluster-robust errors (DS-1000 by original question) : paired comparisons with exact McNemar or paired t, Holm, and letter groups instead of a ranking : delta-method interval on passes per minute, minimum detectable difference per pair
      2026-10-19 (later) : The audit's 34 security findings fixed in one PR : chat shares are snapshots only, Yjs socket handlers removed, Redis required for session revocation : no cross-origin access by default, llama-server on loopback, deleted users' data purged
      2026-10-19 (latest) : The frontend makes UUIDs without crypto.randomUUID, which plain-HTTP pages from the LAN lack : falls back to crypto.getRandomValues
      2026-10-19 (final) : A graded answer passes only when its tests ran to the end : a per-run nonce instead of the exit status, the model's __main__ block no longer run : earlier pass rates not comparable : nothing a grade starts outlives it, grading off the event loop
      2026-10-19 (night) : The Tests page fetches datasets, calibrates the graders and runs one item : one Tests job at a time, never alongside a tune sweep : datasets fetched, DS-1000 456 of 511 gradeable here, every reference verdict unchanged by the new grader
      2026-10-19 (last) : The fingerprint covers the model file, extra arguments and fitting, and llama-server runs with -fit off : every config_id changed once, noted in the database
      2026-10-23 : A backend can stop its served model and benchmark jobs when it exits (LLLM_STOP_JOBS_ON_SHUTDOWN), off by default : make backend's uvicorn flags configurable, so shutdown can't hang on an open stream : stage markers for a supervising app
      2026-10-23 (later) : Desktop app (apps/desktop, Electron, Linux rpm) : loads the backend's own pages, so desktop and browser stay identical : starts the stack when nothing runs and stops what it started, with a step-by-step progress dialog : attaches to a terminal-started stack and leaves it running : one setting moves it to a remote server
      2026-10-23 (latest) : llama.cpp build 10597 built on Fedora with CUDA 13.4.3 and GCC 16 : toolkit from NVIDIA's repo, its driver packages excluded so RPM Fusion's driver stays : nothing served or measured on native Linux yet
    section Near-Term
      "~1 week" : Resolve the blocking rack hole-type question : confirm riser and PSU questions : re-verify current component pricing
      "~2-4 weeks" : Finish the benchmark upgrade : HumanEval+ and MBPP+ replace HumanEval and MBPP : a LiveCodeBench slice with a per-run release-date window : a llama-bench pre-screen driven by Optuna
    section Short-Term
      "~1-2 months" : Purchase and provision the R730 and V100 server : run the five acceptance tests : migrate Qwen3.8-27B to fully VRAM-resident serving
    section Medium-Term
      "~6 months" : Add math and statistics benchmark coverage : stand up Tailscale network exposure : evaluate a second V100 : watch for a Qwen3.8-35B-A3B release : local coding-agent features in the desktop app
    section Long-Term
      "~2 years" : Network-accessible household inference backend behind Local LLM : early groundwork for smart-home integration
